Test PW DFT+U with noncollinear spin (nspin=4), fixed local occupation
matrices, and two ionic relaxation steps.

The reference records this finite two-step workflow with the original
reciprocal-space SCF tolerance of 1e-7. Both electronic SCF cycles must
converge; relax_nmax=2 sets the ionic-step budget. The structure, PBE spin
mapping, pseudopotential, fixed occupation matrices, cutoffs, smearing,
mixing parameters, and SCF stopping condition are unchanged.

This magnetic case is sensitive to diagonalization accuracy. The adaptive
threshold previously became loose again at the start of an electronic
cycle, which changed the forces and the next ionic geometry between
solvers. pw_diag_thr_max=5e-14 now bounds the threshold in every cycle,
including both ionic steps. pw_diag_nmax=500 provides the corresponding
iteration budget. The option defaults to zero for other calculations.

Reference calibration (2026-10-29): GNU 12.3, OpenMPI 5.0.10, double
precision, four MPI processes, OMP_NUM_THREADS=OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1.
result.ref is copied from an independent CG run with pw_diag_thr and
pw_diag_thr_max both set to 1e-20. CG tests its energy decrease, whereas
PPCG tests its residual norm, so the reference uses a separate CG
threshold. Tightening CG from 1e-18 to 1e-20 changes the final energy by
4.67e-8 eV. All reference fields satisfy the existing tolerances in that
comparison.

Against this CG reference, the default Davidson-subspace and PPCG runs
at 5e-14 give the following absolute differences:

solver          energy (eV)   energy/atom (eV)  force sum     stress sum
dav_subspace    5.9501e-8     2.9800e-8         8.0e-6        3.0e-6
ppcg            5.3115e-10    3.0013e-10        0             2.0e-6
original limit  1e-7          1e-7              1e-4          1e-3

Both solvers also pass with one MPI process. All these runs complete
14 and 12 electronic iterations in the two ionic steps, respectively,
without an iterative eigensolver failure. The original collector and
acceptance tolerances are retained. The new reference corresponds to
the explicit accuracy bound; the previous adaptive-threshold reference
had final energy -5652.1157954576747215 eV.

To reproduce, run this directory with a build supporting
pw_diag_thr_max for calculation=relax:

  OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 mpirun -np 4 /path/to/abacus

In a separate copy, change only ks_solver to ppcg for the paired test.
For the independent CG reference, set ks_solver=cg and both
pw_diag_thr and pw_diag_thr_max to 1e-20; retain all other INPUT values.
